op":"eos","text":"To find $\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b})$, we can use the distributive property of the cross product. We have:\n\n\\[\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = 3(\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}) - 2(\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}).\\]\n\nGiven that $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix}$, we can use the property of the cross product $\\mathbf{a} \\times \\mathbf{c} = -(\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a})$ to find $\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a}$. Therefore, \n\n\\[\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{a} = -\\begin{pmatrix} 4 \\\\ 7 \\\\ 2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\nNext, since $\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = \\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix}$, we use $\\mathbf{b} \\times \\mathbf{c} = -(\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b})$ to find $\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b}$:\n\n\\[\\mathbf{c} \\times \\mathbf{b} = -\\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\\\ -7 \\\\ 18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -18 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\nNow we can substitute these results back into the expression for $\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b})$:\n\n\\[\\mathbf{c} \\times (3 \\mathbf{a} - 2 \\mathbf{b}) = 3\\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} - 2\\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -18 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\nWe can now compute this as:\n\n\\[3\\begin{pmatrix} -4 \\\\ -7 \\\\ -2 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix},\\]\n\\[-2\\begin{pmatrix} -1 \\\\ 7 \\\\ -18 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 36 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\nAdding these vectors together:\n\n\\[\\begin{pmatrix} -12 \\\\ -21 \\\\ -6 \\end{pmatrix} + \\begin{pmatrix} 2 \\\\ -14 \\\\ 36 \\end{pmatrix} = \\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}.\\]\n\nSo, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}}.\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\begin{pmatrix} -10 \\\\ -35 \\\\ 30 \\end{pmatrix}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true}}
